WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.129
Chapter five: publishing a paper.

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:08.336
From files on your computer to a listed, citable paper, and then new versions and notices.

00:00:08.336 --> 00:00:13.493
Before you start, check five things. Each one stops a submission if it is missing.

00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:16.038
Only tier two, Author, can start papers.

00:00:16.038 --> 00:00:19.409
You need an endorsement in every category you choose.

00:00:19.409 --> 00:00:24.325
Co-authors copy their DID from the Credentials card on their dashboard.

00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:27.108
The submit page lists anything that blocks you.

00:00:27.108 --> 00:00:31.296
For example, new Author accounts can start one new paper a week.

00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:36.569
You sign and submit. Every co-author consents. A safety scan checks the files.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:42.512
Then a moderator decides. A listed paper gets an AI pre-review and formal reviews.

00:00:42.512 --> 00:00:46.679
The path can stop at three points. A decline stops the version.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.722
A failed scan holds it until you fix the file.

00:00:49.722 --> 00:00:54.091
A hold or rejection gives a reason, and you can appeal once.

00:00:54.091 --> 00:00:56.340
Choose Submit in the navigation bar.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.526
The wizard has five steps, and saves your progress in this browser.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:05.861
After you submit, the draft is cleared. If submitting fails, the draft is kept.

00:01:05.861 --> 00:01:11.410
Step one: files. The Paper zone takes your PDF, LaTeX source and figures.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:15.286
Code and data are optional, as zip or tar archives.

00:01:15.286 --> 00:01:18.955
You need a PDF or LaTeX source to continue.

00:01:18.955 --> 00:01:23.795
A PDF can be up to 50 MiB, and any other file up to 5 GiB.

00:01:23.795 --> 00:01:27.967
Accounts under 90 days old can upload 2 GiB a day.

00:01:27.967 --> 00:01:31.621
Older accounts can upload 20 GiB a day.

00:01:31.621 --> 00:01:37.852
Each file gets a role, such as Paper PDF. Uploads resume after a dropped connection.

00:01:37.852 --> 00:01:41.664
Unfinished uploads are deleted after 24 hours.

00:01:41.664 --> 00:01:42.934
Step two: details.

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:47.873
The title can have up to 300 characters, and the abstract up to 5,000.

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:51.471
Scholium does not read the abstract from your file.

00:01:51.471 --> 00:01:54.693
Choose one to three endorsed categories.

00:01:54.693 --> 00:01:57.014
The default licence is CC BY 4.0.

00:01:57.014 --> 00:02:00.671
Each option says whether journals usually accept it.

00:02:00.671 --> 00:02:04.587
You cannot change the licence of a signed version.

00:02:04.587 --> 00:02:07.838
Step three: authors. You are on the list already.

00:02:07.838 --> 00:02:13.078
Add each co-author by DID, and give everyone at least one CRediT role, you too.

00:02:13.078 --> 00:02:15.867
Move up and Move down set the order.

00:02:15.867 --> 00:02:21.708
Use DIDs. In this release, Scholium cannot find an account by ORCID iD or email.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:29.045
Such an author shows Not matched, and blocks the step until you remove them or add them by DID.

00:02:29.045 --> 00:02:31.402
Step four lists the automated checks.

00:02:31.402 --> 00:02:36.752
They run after you sign and every co-author consents, so here they show Not run yet.

00:02:36.752 --> 00:02:38.235
You can continue.

00:02:38.235 --> 00:02:42.294
Step five: sign. Review the summary. You are signing version one.

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:47.189
You cannot edit it later, but you can publish a new version at any time.

00:02:47.189 --> 00:02:48.652
Choose Sign and submit.

00:02:48.652 --> 00:02:54.884
Your device signs the paper, its file list and its first version, so expect three passkey prompts.

00:02:54.884 --> 00:02:57.573
Then you see Submitted, version one.

00:02:57.573 --> 00:03:03.149
The status tracker shows each stage as Done, In progress, Needs attention or Not started.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:07.808
You must consent too. A Sign your consent button stays until you do.

00:03:07.808 --> 00:03:11.066
Nobody can be published as an author without agreeing.

00:03:11.066 --> 00:03:16.294
Every author gets a notification, and an email if they have a confirmed address.

00:03:16.294 --> 00:03:22.429
On the Review and sign page, you can add a public comment, then accept or decline authorship.

00:03:22.429 --> 00:03:28.107
A decline asks you to confirm. The files open only after the safety scan passes.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:31.844
If everyone accepts, the version goes to the safety scan.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:37.351
If anyone declines, it returns to draft and names who declined. It cannot ask again.

00:03:37.351 --> 00:03:41.947
Fix the author list and submit a new version. Answers are final.

00:03:41.947 --> 00:03:46.016
Scholium inspects your files before anyone can open them.

00:03:46.016 --> 00:03:55.583
It checks PDFs for embedded JavaScript and files, actions that launch programs, hidden text, and text that tries to instruct AI tools.

00:03:55.583 --> 00:03:58.411
Encrypted or unreadable PDFs fail.

00:03:58.411 --> 00:04:03.586
Archives are checked for unsafe paths, links and malware. Files are never changed.

00:04:03.586 --> 00:04:08.130
If a file fails, the version is held, and the tracker shows what failed.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.928
Fix the file and submit a new version.

00:04:10.928 --> 00:04:13.566
At moderation, Scholium runs three checks.

00:04:13.566 --> 00:04:19.243
You and the moderators see the results before listing, and everyone sees them after.

00:04:19.243 --> 00:04:24.841
Similarity reports the highest overlap of five-word phrases with any listed paper.

00:04:24.841 --> 00:04:31.248
Under 15 percent is Low overlap, from 15 percent Worth a look, and from 30 percent High.

00:04:31.248 --> 00:04:35.037
References reports how many references could be resolved.

00:04:35.037 --> 00:04:38.760
Metadata match checks for your signed title on page one.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.948
High similarity and unresolved references do not block listing.

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:46.539
A failed file or a title mismatch must be fixed.

00:04:46.539 --> 00:04:54.652
A volunteer moderator reviews every new version, with a target of 48 hours, and can list, hold, reclassify or reject it.

00:04:54.652 --> 00:05:00.528
Every decision names a policy clause and a reason, and is a public signed record.

00:05:00.528 --> 00:05:05.273
If your paper is held or rejected, the first author gets a notification.

00:05:05.273 --> 00:05:09.687
The paper page shows the reason, and says that you can appeal once.

00:05:09.687 --> 00:05:12.064
Chapter nine explains appeals.

00:05:12.064 --> 00:05:16.465
A listed paper has a permanent ID, and each version has its own.

00:05:16.465 --> 00:05:22.640
The ID ends in a checksum, so typos are caught. A search for the ID opens the paper.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:27.978
The paper appears in the feed, its category, search, Atom feeds and daily digests.

00:05:27.978 --> 00:05:31.493
The AI pre-review starts, and reviewers can review it.

00:05:31.493 --> 00:05:34.496
Invite reviewer points a reviewer at it.

00:05:34.496 --> 00:05:38.626
Papers are never edited. Choose New version on your paper page.

00:05:38.626 --> 00:05:41.249
The form starts from the latest version.

00:05:41.249 --> 00:05:46.566
Keep or replace files, write the required change note, and sign and submit.

00:05:46.566 --> 00:05:52.490
The new version goes through consent, the scan and moderation again, with the same author list.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:56.544
Earlier versions stay available, and show A newer version exists.

00:05:56.544 --> 00:06:00.811
The latest version's authors, or a moderator, can publish one.

00:06:00.811 --> 00:06:05.376
To add a notice, use Issue notice on the paper page and give a reason.

00:06:05.376 --> 00:06:10.406
Any author, or a moderator, can issue one. It applies to every version.

00:06:10.406 --> 00:06:13.670
A correction notes an error, but the work stands.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:17.667
A retraction says readers should no longer rely on the work.

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:22.597
The status becomes Corrected or Retracted, with a banner on every version.

00:06:22.597 --> 00:06:25.462
A retraction also shows in citations.

00:06:25.462 --> 00:06:28.826
A withdrawal says you no longer stand behind the paper.

00:06:28.826 --> 00:06:34.025
A banner shows your reason, the status does not change, and the files stay available.

00:06:34.025 --> 00:06:38.768
Retraction and withdrawal ask you to confirm. You cannot undo a notice.

00:06:38.768 --> 00:06:41.729
Moderators can mirror paper details from arXiv.

00:06:41.729 --> 00:06:49.942
In this release, imports work through the API only, and you cannot yet claim an imported paper as its author in the web app.

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:54.445
In short: check your tier, endorsements and co-author DIDs first.

00:06:54.445 --> 00:06:57.701
Every author consents, and a moderator decides.

00:06:57.701 --> 00:07:01.373
To change a paper, publish a new version or a notice.

00:07:01.373 --> 00:07:04.336
Next, chapter six: reviewing a paper.
